{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Reduce SSAI costs using new features in AWS Elemental MediaTailor | AWS for M&E Blog","context":"## AWS for M&E Blog\n\n# Reduce SSAI costs using new features in AWS Elemental MediaTailor\n\nYour streaming content is taking off, viewership is soaring and ad revenue is increasing. However, the costs of monitoring all those streaming sessions, and remaining operational, are also increasing. Sound familiar? Streaming services face this challenge every day as they scale their server-side ad insertion (SSAI) streaming operations.\n\nWe are excited to share how Amazon Web Services (AWS) Elemental MediaTailor (MediaTailor) is addressing this challenge with two dedicated features that put the decision-making power back in your hands. We will demonstrate how using MediaTailor for SSAI workflows can help minimize spending, while maintaining overall visibility into their channels’ health and uptime, as you gain insights on your SSAI fill rates","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/media/reduce-ssai-costs-using-new-features-in-aws-elemental-mediatailor/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Troubleshoot MediaTailor SSAI with CDNs for uninterrupted ad delivery","context":"## Advanced troubleshooting\n\nFor more complex issues, try these advanced troubleshooting techniques:\n\nInconsistent ad targeting behavior\n: Check for query parameter inconsistencies between player requests and ADS\n requests. Ensure all required targeting parameters are properly passed\n through the CDN.\n\nCDN cache inconsistencies\n: Verify cache key configurations to ensure proper content differentiation.\n Consider implementing cache purging for critical manifest updates.\n\nAd tracking failures\n: Check that beacon URLs are properly forwarded and not blocked by the CDN.\n Verify that client players can reach the tracking endpoints","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/mediatailor/latest/ug/troubleshooting-ssai-cdn.html"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"Troubleshooting MediaTailor event flow issues","context":"### Ad decision server request failures\n\n**Symptoms:** Event flow stops after ad\nopportunity detection. No ADS request events logged.\n\n**Common causes and solutions**\n\n* **ADS URL configuration errors:** Verify\n the ADS URL in your playback configuration is correct and accessible. In\n the ads interaction log, you will see an ADS request event\n (`MAKING_ADS_REQUEST`) but no corresponding VAST\n response, often accompanied by an `ERROR_UNKNOWN` or similar\n error event.\n* **Network connectivity issues:** Check\n network connectivity between MediaTailor and your ADS, including firewall\n rules and DNS resolution.\n* **SSL/TLS certificate problems:** Ensure\n your ADS uses valid SSL certificates from a trusted certificate\n authority. For Google Ad Manager specifically, you might need to\n contact AWS Support to enable a configuration flag that accepts Google's\n SSL certificates.\n\n**Diagnostic query**\n\nThe following query helps diagnose ADS request failures by tracking the event\nsequence:\n\n```\nfields @timestamp, eventType, sessionId\n| filter sessionId = \"your-session-id\"\n| filter eventType in [\"AD_MARKER_FOUND\", \"MAKING_ADS_REQUEST\", \"ERROR_ADS_IO\", \"ERROR_UNKNOWN_HOST\"]\n| sort @timestamp asc\n```","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/mediatailor/latest/ug/troubleshooting-event-flow.html"}]}}

## Recent AWS announcements (What's New)

Newer than your training data may be. When these conflict with the documentation results above or with what you remember, prefer the most recent dated source.

{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now offers Yield Optimization to automatically fill ad breaks with Amazon Ads demand - AWS","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor has introduced a new feature called Yield Optimization, which automatically monetizes unused ad inventory during server-side ad insertion (SSAI) for livestreams. This capability is exclusive to publishers in the Amazon Publisher Services (APS) Streaming TV program and comes at no additional cost. Yield optimization turns unfilled ad breaks into monetized impressions, enabling publishers to maximize their revenue without requiring any extra infrastructure or client-side changes.\n\nThe feature is designed for large-scale live events, ensuring low latency and fast response times during peak viewership. Ads are stitched directly into the stream, ensuring seamless playback on every device. Publishers have control over which ads run in their streams by setting their own price floors and category rules.\n\nYield optimization is available in all AWS Regions where MediaTailor is available, including US East (Ohio), US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), Africa (Cape Town), Asia Pacific (Hyderabad, Malaysia, Melbourne, Mumbai, Osaka, Seoul, Singapore, Sydney, Tokyo), Canada (Central), Europe (Frankfurt, Ireland, London, Paris, Stockholm), Middle East (UAE), and South America (São Paulo). Publishers can monitor ad fill rate improvements using MediaTailor metrics in Amazon CloudWatch and track revenue and earnings through the APS Publisher portal","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/mediatailor-yield-optimization/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now provides automatic secure server-to-server integration with Google's ad platforms - AWS","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor has updated its service to automatically establish secure, authenticated server-to-server connections with Google's ad platforms: Google Ad Manager (GAM), Google Campaign Manager (GCM), and Google Display & Video 360 (DV360). This integration is designed to provide a seamless experience for MediaTailor customers using these ad platforms. MediaTailor offers server-side ad insertion (SSAI) to personalize ads in video streams, which requires secure, authenticated connections when making ad requests and firing ad tracking events. Previously, customers had to request activation of this integration through an AWS support case and be added to an allow list. With this update, MediaTailor automatically detects requests destined for Google's ad servers and establishes the required secure connection without customer intervention.\n\nFor Google Ad Manager, server-side ad requests to Google's ad server for publishers are automatically secured, which is necessary for access to Authorized Buyers, Google's real-time ad sales marketplace and ad exchange. For Google Campaign Manager and DV360, server-side impression tracking requests are automatically routed through Google's authenticated endpoint and secured, supporting advertisers who run campaigns on these platforms with more accurate reporting and fewer rejected impressions. All other ad requests continue to operate without modification.\n\nThis automatic server-to-server Google integration is available in all AWS Regions where MediaTailor is available, including US East (Ohio), US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon); Africa (Cape Town); Asia Pacific (Hyderabad, Malaysia, Melbourne, Mumbai, Osaka, Seoul, Singapore, Sydney, Tokyo); Canada (Central); Europe (Frankfurt, Ireland, London, Paris, Stockholm); Middle East (UAE); and South America (São Paulo). There is no additional cost for this feature. For more information, visit the AWS Elemental MediaTailor documentation","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/05/mediatailor-automatic-google-ad-platform-integration/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now supports ad trickplay personalization and compact DASH manifest optimization via dynamic transcoding - AWS","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor has introduced new features for ad personalization and compact DASH manifest optimization through dynamic transcoding. Previously, these capabilities required custom transcoding profiles. MediaTailor, which provides server-side ad insertion, now supports trickplay personalization for HLS and DASH workflows. This ensures that advertisements include trickplay variants and associated image streams that align with origin content specifications, delivering a consistent viewer experience. MediaTailor also supports compact DASH manifests, which elevate the SegmentTemplate element from individual Representation elements to the AdaptationSet level, reducing overall manifest size for more efficient delivery and improved compatibility. These features are available in all regions where MediaTailor is available, including 17 regions in North and South America, Europe, Asia Pacific, and the Middle East. There is no additional cost for this feature","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/05/mediatail-ad-trickplay-and-compact-dash-manifest-optimization/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now supports Low-Latency HLS ad insertion - AWS","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now supports low-latency HTTP Live Streaming (LL-HLS) ad insertion using HLS Interstitials. MediaTailor is a service for video providers to monetize live streams, linear channels, and video-on-demand content. LL-HLS reduces live latency by delivering partial segments and keeping media playlists cacheable at CDN edges. MediaTailor uses HLS Interstitials to reference ads as separate playlists, allowing for low-latency playback at scale and moving ad decision server calls off the manifest request path. This capability is ideal for live sports, news, betting and wagering, watch-party, and interactive live formats. Low-latency HLS ad insertion is available in all AWS Regions where MediaTailor is available. For more information, visit the MediaTailor product page and server-guided ad insertion documentation. To get started, sign in to the MediaTailor console. MediaTailor supports LL-HLS by delivering partial segments and keeping media playlists cacheable at CDN edges, using HLS Interstitials to reference ads as separate playlists, and moving ad decision server calls off the manifest request path. This results in low-latency playback at scale, making it suitable for live events and interactive formats where latency is crucial. The feature is currently available in all AWS Regions where MediaTailor is offered. For further details, interested parties can refer to the MediaTailor product page and server-guided ad insertion documentation and sign in to the MediaTailor console to get started","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/aws-elemental-mediatailor-low-latency-hls-ad-insertion/"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"aws-marketplace-metering","skill_description":"Deploys, queries, and debugs AWS Marketplace usage-based (PAYG) metering — the pipeline (ResolveCustomer, BatchMeterUsage, EventBridge via SAM) and querying/debugging metering records, statuses, failures, discrepancies. Covers Concurrent Agreements (CustomerAWSAccountId + LicenseArn), multi-product, CloudTrail Event History (90 days; never CloudTrail Lake), Seller Reports (Billed Revenue/Usage columns + CSV/SDDS parsing), existing-stack detection, metering region for BatchMeterUsage/MeterUsage (DisabledApiException), metered AMI/Container + IAM roles, where registration data lives (customer-profile table), legacy ProductCode + CustomerIdentifier, DuplicateRecord/CustomerNotSubscribed, bad LicenseArn. Also SCOPES adjacent asks — flat-rate/SaaS-Subscription \"do I still meter\", CCP included-units + overage, contract term/annual renewal, forecasting future bills/usage — with the right answer or a one-line redirect. Use for any BatchMeterUsage/ResolveCustomer or SaaS usage-billing question.\n\nServices: aws-marketplace, marketplace-metering\nTasks: deploy, integrate, query, debug, troubleshoot, analyze\nPersona: developer\nWorkload: saas\n*","skill_name":"aws-marketplace-metering"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Look up AWS docs on MediaTailor SSAI identical-ads troubleshooting guidance."}
